        <mxCell id="si_ai_note" parent="1" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=10;fontColor=#666666;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="Chunk Processor and Document Generator are separate Container Apps from the core API (different workload shape - see ARCHITECTURE.md &#167;7), sharing the same Container Registry. Together with Document Intelligence, AI Search, Azure OpenAI and this Blob Storage they form ONE shared 'Document Generation Platform' resource group, separate from the core service's rg-country-package-core - a document-generation-with-approvals capability other WBG operational processes (e.g. MDB project-proposal generation) can reuse over time, reached only through Private Endpoints (internal use only). Two resource groups total; a further split is a later decision once there is a second real consumer, not a day-one default. An RG boundary here is a management boundary, never a network trust boundary." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="70" width="990" x="-260" y="900" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
